          "tz": 180
        },
        "subject": "LU-20769 lfsck: flush signals before sending RPC",
        "message": "LU-20769 lfsck: flush signals before sending RPC\n\nlfsck uses signal SIGINT to stop assistent threads, then those\nassistent threads notifiy lfsck on other nodes (like OSTs) using\ndedicated RPCs, but ptlrpc_set_wait() sets rq_allow_intr=1 and then:\n\n\tif (signal_pending(current))\n\t\tremaining = -EINTR;\n...\n\t} else if (remaining < 0) {\n\t\trc = -EINTR;\n\t\tptlrpc_interrupted_set(set);\n\ni.e. ptlrpc doesn't even try to send RPC and remote lfsck instances\nkeep going leading subsequent subtest failures.\n\nthe fix is to flush pending signals in lfsck's stop path.\n\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Alex Zhuravlev <bzzz@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I4f8dff802a458a72a13df9a5d19e02f80d42153e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
